hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1788,"and he had four braids. \\n\\n[Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Gharib. Muhammad said: I do not know of Mujahid (a narrator) hearing from Umm Hani. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1781 Arabic Hadees: 1781\""1789""","Narrated Abu Sa'eed - who is 'Abdullah bin Busr: \I heard Abu Kabshah Al-Anmari saying: 'The Kimam (caps) of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were Buthan (stretched over the head).'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Munkar"""
1790,"Narrated Hudhaifa: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took hold of the calf of my shin - or his shin - and he said: \""This is the place of the Izar"""
1791,"Narrated Abu Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Rukanah: From his father that Rukanah wrestled the Prophet (ﷺ) and the Prophet (ﷺ) won the match. Rukanah said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Indeed what distinguishes between us and between the idolater is the turban over the cap.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. Its chain is not established"""
1792,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Buraidah: From his father who said: \A man wearing an iron ring came to the Prophet (ﷺ). So he said to him: 'What is this I see on you"""
1793,"Narrated Ibn Abi Musa: \I heard 'Ali saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited Al-Qassi"""
1794,"Narrated Anas: \The garment the Messenger (ﷺ) like most to wear was the Hibrah.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"""
1795,"Qutaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, he said: \Al-Hasan and al-Husayn used to wear rings on their left hands.\"" And this is a hasan sahih hadith."""
1796,"Narrated Hisham b. Zaid: \I heard Anas saying: 'Once we provoked a rabbit at Marr Az-Zahran. So the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rushed after it"""
1797,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about eating a mastigure and he said: 'I do not eat it"""
1798,"Narrated Ibn Abi 'Ammar: \I asked Jabir: 'Is badger kind of game animal?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Should I eat it?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" He said: 'I said: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say that ?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Some of the people of knowledge followed this. They did not see any harm eating badger. This is the view of Ahmad and Ishaq. A Hadith has been related from the Prophet (ﷺ) indicating disapproval of eating badger but its chain is not strong. Some of the people of knowledge disliked eating badger. This is the view of Ibn Al-Mubarak. Yahya bin Al-Qattan said: \""Jarir bin Hazm reported this Hadith from 'Abdullah bin 'Ubaid bin 'Umair"""
1799,"Narrated Khuzaimah bin Jaz': \I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about eating badger. He said: 'Does anyone eat badger?' So I asked him about eating wolf' He said: 'Does anyone who has any good in him eat wolf?'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] The chain for this Hadith is not strong. We do not know of it except as a narration of Isma'il bin Muslim from 'Abdul-Karim Abi Umayyah. Some of the people of Hadith have criticized Isma'il and 'Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah. And he is 'Abdul-Karim bin Qais"""
1800,"Narrated Jabir: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) allowed us to eat horse meat"""
1801,"# Scholarly Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Chain of Narration:**\n\nAḥmad ibn Manīʿ narrated to us, Rawḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abū al-Zubayr informed me, from Jābir, who said:\n\n**Text of the Hadith:**\n\n> The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited images (aṣ-ṣuwar) in the house, and He ﷺ prohibited that such things be made.\n\n**Additional Narrations:**\n\nHe (the narrator) said: And in this chapter (there are narrations) from ʿAlī, Abū Ṭalḥah, ʿĀʾishah, Abū Hurayrah, and Abū Ayyūb (may Allah be pleased with them all).\n\n**Grading:**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: The Ḥadīth of Jābir is a Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ Ḥadīth.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:**\n\n- **aṣ-ṣuwar** (الصُّوْرَةِ): Refers to images or figures of animate beings, which the Prophet ﷺ forbade from being present in the home and prohibited from being created.\n- **Ḥasan Ṣaḥī"
1802,"Narrated Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushani: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the pots of Zorastrians. He said: 'Clean them by washing them"""
1803,"Narrated Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushani: That he said: \O Messenger of Allah! We live in a land of the People of Book and we cook in their containers"""
1804,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: From Maimunah that a mouse fell in some cooking fat and died. So the Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about that and he said: \Remove it (the mouse) and what was around it and then eat it (the fat).\"" He said: There are something on this topic from Abu Hurairah. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. This Hadith has been related from Az-Zuhri"""
1805,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Let none of you wat with his left hand nor drink with his left hand"""
1806,"Humayd ibn Mas‘adah narrated to us, ‘Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was of medium stature, neither tall nor short. He had a handsome body and was of brown complexion. His hair was neither tightly curled nor completely straight. When he walked, he would lean slightly forward.\n\nHe (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there are also narrations from ‘A’ishah, al-Bara’, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn ‘Abbas, Abu Sa‘id, Jabir, Wa’il ibn Hujr, and Umm Hani’ رضي الله"
1807,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you eats"""
1808,"Narrated Jabir: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When one of you eats food"""
1809,"Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, with this chain of transmission, a similar narration.\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. He also said: In this chapter, there is also a narration from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
1810,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn Humayd, narrated to us Abu Dawud, who is at-Tayalisi, from 'Abbad ibn Mansur, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Use kohl made from ithmid"," for it clears the vision and promotes hair growth.\"" It is also reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had a kohl container with which he would apply kohl every night", three times in one eye and three times in the other. This hadith has been narrated through various chains of transmission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)," who said: \""You should use kohl made from ithmid"," for it clears the vision and promotes hair growth.\"" Abu 'Isa said: The hadith of Ibn 'Abbas is a good hadith; we do not know it in this wording except from the hadith of 'Abbad ibn Mansur."""
1811,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the blessing descends to the middle of the food"""
1812,"Narrated Jabir: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever eats from these - the first time"""
1813,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was staying with Abu Ayyub. When he ate some food"""
1814,"Narrated Sharik bin Hanbal:That 'Ali said: \Eating garlic was prohibited except when cooked"""
1815,"Narrated Sharik bin Hanbal:That 'Ali said: \Eating garlic is no good"""
1816,Narrated 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Burdah: From his father that Umm Ayyub informed him that the Prophet (ﷺ) had stayed with them
1817,"Narrated Abu Khaldah:That Abu Al-'Aliyah said: \garlic is among the good provisions.\"" Abu Khaldah's name is Khalid bin Dinar"""
1818,"It was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr, who reported from al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā, from ʿAbd al-Muʾmin ibn Khālid, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from Umm Salamah (may Allāh be pleased with her), who said:\n\n\The garment most beloved to the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) was the qamīṣ (shirt).\"""""
1819,"Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Ṣawwāf al-Baṣrī narrated to us, Mu‘ādh ibn Hishām al-Dastawā’ī narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Budayl ibn Maysarah al-‘Uqaylī, from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Asmā’ bint Yazīd ibn al-Sakān al-Anṣāriyyah, who said: \The sleeve of the Messenger of Allah", peace and blessings be upon him," used to reach the wrist.\"" Abū ‘Īsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith."""
1820,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited taking two dates at a time until seeking permission from one's companion.\"" He said: There is something on this topic from Sa'd the freed slave of Abu Bakr. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
1821,"Narrated 'Aishah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \A house without dates"""
1822,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah is pleased with the slave who"""
1823,"Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took the hand of a leper and put it in the Qas'ah. Then he said: 'Eat in Allah's Name"""
1824,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The disbeliever eats with seven intestines and the believer eats with one intestine.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. He said: There are narrations on this topic from Abu Hurairah"""
1825,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a disbeliever as a guest. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered that a sheep be milked so he could drink. Then another was milked so he could drink"""
1826,"Narrated Abu Ya'fur Al-'Abdi: That 'Abdullah bin Abi Awfa was asked about locust. He said: \I participated in six military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (saws"""
1827,"Narrated Abu Ya'fur: That Ibn Abi Awfa said: \We participated in seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
1828,"Narrated At-Taimi: From Jabir bin 'Abdullah and Anas bin Malik who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated against locusts he would say: 'O Allah! Destroy the locusts"""
1829,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited eating the Jallalah and milking it.\"" He said: There is something on this topic from 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. Ath-Thawri reported it from Ibn Abi Najih"""
1830,"Narrated Zahdam Al-Jarmi: \I entered upon Abu Musa while he was eating chicken"""
1831,"Narrated Zahdam: From Abu Musa who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eating chicken meat.\"" He said: The Hadith has more statements that this. And this Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Ayyub As-Sakhtiyani also reported this Hadith from Al-Qasim At-Tamimi"""
1832,"Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had sandals with two straps. Abu Isa (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. He also said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
1833,Narrated Umm Salamah: That she brought a side of roasted meat to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
1834,"Narrated Abu Juhaidah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \As for me"""
1835,"Narrated 'Aishah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) liked sweets and honey.\"" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. 'Ali bin Mus-hir reported it from Hisham bin 'Urwah"""
1836,"Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Dinar, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli, a Kufan, narrated to us Huraam ibn Sufyan al-Bajali al-Kufi, from al-Layth, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: \Sometimes the Prophet (peace be upon him) would walk with only one sandal on.\"""""
1837,"Narrated Abu Dharr: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let one of you not consider any good to be insignificant. If he has nothing"""
1838,"Narrated Abu Musa: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Many a man achieved perfection"""
1839,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Al-Harith: \My father had me married so he invited people"""
1840,Narrated Ja'far bin 'Amr bin Umayyah Ad-Damri: From his father who said that he saw the Prophet (ﷺ) making incisions (with a knife) into a piece of a lamb shoulder which he ate from
1841,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: \Some meat was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) and a foreleg was presented to him"""
1842,"Narrated 'Aishah: \The foreleg was not the part of the meat that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) liked most"""
1843,"Narrated Jabir: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \What an excellent condiment vinegar is"""
1844,"Narrated 'Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \What an excellent condiment vinegar is.\"" Another chain with similar except that he (ﷺ) said: \""What an excellent condiment"""
1845,"Narrated Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and said: 'Do you have anything?' I said: 'No"""
1846,"Narrated Jabir: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \What an excellent condiment vinegar is.\"" There are narrations on this topic from 'Aishah and Umm Hani'"""
1847,"Narrated 'Aishah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) would eat melon with fresh dates.\"" He said: There is something on about this from Anas. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. Some of them reported it form Hisham bin 'Urwah from his father in Mursal form from the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
1848,"Narrated Jabir: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \What an excellent condiment vinegar is.\"" There are narrations on this topic from 'Aishah and Umm Hani'"""
1849,"Narrated 'Aishah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) would eat melon with fresh dates.\"" He said: There is something on about this from Anas. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. Some of them reported it form Hisham bin 'Urwah from his father in Mursal form from the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
1850,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Ja'far: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would eat snake cucumber with fresh dates. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"""
1851,"""I asked Jabir: 'Is badger kind of game animal?' He said: 'Yes.'"" He said: ""I said: 'Should I eat it?' He said: 'Yes.'"" He said: 'I said: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say that ?' He said: 'Yes.'""


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih.


Some of the people of knowledge followed this. They did not see any harm eating badger. This is the view of Ahmad and Ishaq. A Hadith has been related from the Prophet (ﷺ) indicating disapproval of eating badger but its chain is not strong. Some of the people of knowledge disliked eating badger. This is the view of Ibn Al-Mubarak. Yahya bin Al-Qattan said: ""Jarir bin Hazm reported this Hadith from 'Abdullah bin 'Ubaid bin 'Umair, from Ibn Abi 'Ammar, from Jabir, from 'Umar, as his saying. And the narration of Ibn Juraij (a narrator in the chain of this Hadith) is more correct. And Ibn Abi 'Ammar is 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Abi 'Ammar Al-Makki."
1852,"Narrated Salman: \I read in the Tawrah that the blessing for food is in the Wudu' after it. So I mentioned that to the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
1853,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cae out from the toilet and some food was brought to him. They said: 'Shall we bring you some water for Wudu'?' He said: 'I have only been ordered to perform Wudu' when standing for Salat.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan [Sahih]. 'Amr bin Dinar has reported it from Sa'eed bin Al-Huwairith"""
1854,"Narrated 'Ikrash bin Dhu'aib: \Banu Murrah bin 'Ubaid sent me to bring the Sadaqah from their wealth of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I arrived with him in Al-Madinah and found him sitting between the Muhajirin and the Ansar.\"" He said: \""Then he took my hand and brought me to the home of Umm Salamah and he said: 'Do you have any food?' So a bowl containing a lot of Tharid with pieces of meat was brought to us"""
1855,"Narrated Abu Talut: \I entered upon Anas bin Malik while he was eating gourd"""
1856,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taking from the sides around the dish - meaning the gourd. Since then I still like it.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. This Hadith has been reported through more than one route from Anas bin Malik"""
1857,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ṭā'ī narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Shu'bah related from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū Tha'labah, who said:**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the cooking vessels of the Magians (Majūs). He ﷺ said: **\Clean them by washing"," and cook in them.\""** And he ﷺ forbade every predatory animal possessing fangs.\n\nAbū 'Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: *\""This is a well-known (mashhūr) hadith from the hadith of Abū Tha'labah", and it has been narrated from him through other chains as well. Abū Tha'labah's name is Jurthum, and it is also said Jurhum," and it is also said Nāshib. And this hadith has also been mentioned from Abū Qilābah from Abū Asmā' al-Raḥabī from Abū Tha'labah.\""*\n\n---\n\n**Note:** This hadith addresses the permissibility of using vessels belonging to the Magians (Zoroastrians) after thorough washing"," and simultaneously conveys the Prophet's ﷺ prohibition of consuming predatory animals with fangs."""
1858,# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we are in a land of the People of the Book," so we cook in their pots and drink from their vessels.\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""If you find no other vessels"," then wash them with water.\""**\n\nThen he said: \""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ", we are in a land of game hunting," so what should we do?\""\n\nHe ﷺ said: **\""If you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah", and it kills, then eat. If it is not a trained dog, then if it is slaughtered properly, then eat. And if you shoot with your arrow and mention the name of Allah, and it kills," then eat.\""**\n\n---\n\n**Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan sahih* hadith.\n\n---\n\n### Notes on the Translation:\n\n- **"""
1859,"from the Prophet (ﷺ) and sometimes he reported it indicating doubt, saying: I think it is from 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). And sometimes he said: From Zaid bin Aslam, from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a Mursal form. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1851 Arabic Hadees: 1851\""1860""","Narrated Abu Asid: \The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Eat of its oil and use it (the olives)"""
